    "id": "pose_08_tuck_jump_arms_up",
    "name": "Tuck jump, arms raised",
    "description": "In the air with both feet about 16 cm off the floor. Both knees pulled up and bent with the feet pointed, arms raised in a wide V above the shoulders with open hands, chin slightly up. Left/right are the character's own.",
    "targetModels": [
      "female",
      "male"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Airborne: the lowest vertex is ~0.16 m above the floor (female 155 mm, male 165 mm). The jump height is kept low so the raised hands stay inside the standard preview frame.",
      "Authored on rig/female.glb; the male uses the same rotations and the hips-height-relative root offset. The root height is the mean of the female and male heights that put the contact on y = 0, so both models land within a few millimetres of the floor."
    ],
    "generator": "/tmp/pose-author/build_all.py + p0N.py (poser authoring scripts, kept outside the repository)"
  },
